Now create a shared data prep partial? Each template can include `partials/setup.blade.php` that defines variables. Since Blade `@include` variables leak into parent scope? Yes, included view's variables are available... Actually variables defined with `@php` in an included view do not automatically propagate back to the parent scope? In Blade, includes are rendered with `render()` in a separate scope; variables set inside the include are not available in the parent. So no. Instead, put the setup php directly in each index. Or use a Blade component. Simplest: each index has a small `@php` block at top. 8x ~25 lines is fine.

