Now melati.js with unique petal animation + parallax.

Need to not create petals over reduced motion. Use CSS classes `.mel-petal` defined in CSS. I didn't define. Add CSS for petal via JS inline styles or append CSS in melati.css. Better create elements with class and add CSS to melati.css. Let me append to CSS later with edit. Petals: small white/gold blurred oval falling. Use fixed container `.mel-petals` pointer-events none z-index 90 (above main, below cover? cover z 100; petals z 85 visible after open). Generate 14 petals with random left, delay, duration, size. Use CSS keyframes.

Also parallax cover image on scroll—cover is fixed; only while cover open. Could add pointer parallax: move image slightly with mouse. Simple and subtle.

melati.js:
```js
